<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!-- Standalone parent for qits-artifacts — the ENV-SCOPED HOSTED BYTE PLANE
         (byte-plane-split-plan.md phase 4): hosted npm, maven and OCI registries, published docs
         bundles, the platform's daemon binaries, CI media, and the pin-based garbage collection over
         all of them.

         What is NOT here any more, and where it went:
           - the pull-through caches (NPM_PROXY, MAVEN_PROXY, OCI_MIRROR, their upstreams and the
             access-tracked eviction GC) -> qits-platform-mirror, the one platform-scoped byte
             service;
           - the git smart-HTTP host (`git-storage` and eu.wohlben.qits.githost) -> qits-githost,
             an env service of its own: a repository is not an artifact, it only shared the storage
             layout;
           - the content-addressed blob core and the three registry protocols -> the shared
             libraries qits-blobstore and qits-registries-{common,npm,maven,oci}, which this repo
             now CONSUMES rather than contains.

         Blobs reference qits branches and flows by *string metadata*, never by foreign key, so this
         context never breaks when qits' schema moves. `artifacts` owns its OWN named datasource +
         Flyway lineage — carried over unsquashed and unchanged by the split (migration-plan.md §7,
         "own lineage, unaffected"). The libraries deliberately carry no migrations: each consuming
         service owns its schema.

         DELIBERATELY ITS OWN GAV, following qits-workspaces rather than the qits-workspace-daemon
         extraction which kept eu.wohlben:qits so its children's <parent> resolved unchanged. That
         works when the child artifactIds are globally unique (`workspace-daemon`); it does NOT work
         here, where the module is `artifacts`. Installing eu.wohlben:artifacts:1.0.0-SNAPSHOT would
         clobber the monorepo's jar in the shared ~/.m2 — and in the qits_shared_m2 volume every
         workspace container mounts. The directories stay artifacts/ and service/; only the
         coordinates are namespaced.

         Versions that must stay in step with qits (Quarkus platform, JDK release, MapStruct, Lombok,
         JGit) are duplicated here on purpose: a clone of THIS repo alone must build, with no
         monorepo and no parent to inherit from.

         Trimmed to what these modules actually need. The monorepo's app-wide machinery is
         intentionally omitted: spotless, the :8080 dev-mode port guard, isolated-test surefire
         chunking, enforcer, the derive-fixture-bares antrun step, the maven build-cache extension,
         and the mandatory -Dqits.variant=oauth|forwardauth|local auth profiles. -->
    <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
    <artifactId>qits-artifacts</artifactId>
    <version>2026.905.221813</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>
    <name>qits-artifacts</name>

    <modules>
        <!-- Every library before the app. `artifacts` is what did NOT move out to qits-blobstore or
             qits-registries: the docs and daemon registries, the store explorer, the live blob
             census, the seeder, and the Flyway lineage. `gc` sits after it because it depends on it
             — one way, never back. `service` is the deployable. -->
        <module>artifacts</module>
        <module>gc</module>
        <module>service</module>
    </modules>

    <properties>
        <qits.auth-core.version>2026.905.91442</qits.auth-core.version>
        <!-- The two shared libraries the byte plane was carved into. Published from their own
             repositories (libs/qits-blobstore, libs/qits-registries) and consumed here like any
             other artifact.

             The blob store's only backend is PostgreSQL now, and every consumer moved with it in the
             same campaign. That campaign has released, so both are pinned at their calver. The two
             move together: qits-registries is built against this blobstore.
             ONE VERSION FOR BOTH since 2026.830.175757: the store builds inside the qits-registries
             reactor and ships on its version. The coordinate is unchanged, the config keys are
             unchanged, and the store's packages are eu.wohlben.qits.blobstore.* — so the pins
             cannot be moved one at a time. -->
        <qits.blobstore.version>2026.905.211257</qits.blobstore.version>
        <qits.registries.version>2026.905.211257</qits.registries.version>
        <!-- The platform's datasource resilience baseline: qits-db-core carries PatientPgDriver,
             which the datasource block in the artifacts jar's microprofile-config.properties names,
             and DbRetry. Published by libs/qits-integrations-quarkus, so it is one of the few
             dependencies here that is neither on Maven Central nor in the Quarkus platform — see
             the <repositories> block below. It also arrives transitively on qits-blobstore; it is
             named here because this repository's own config names the driver class. -->
        <qits.db-core.version>2026.905.91442</qits.db-core.version>
        <!-- The user-story framework (test scope): the 21 story classes and
             TokenValidationBootstrapIT are userflows, so a `mvn verify` also regenerates
             service/target/userstories/ — the stories' documentation, network diagrams and
             command transcripts included. 2026.829.153120 carried the Commands facade the story
             chains run their real CLIs through; this repo was its first consumer.

             2026.829.201516 is the release in which the network became PASSIVE:
             Interactions.happened() is gone, an edge is OBSERVED by a tap (a RestAssured filter, a
             mock's recording, this service's own access log) and drained by the framework at story
             end. Two things in it this repo consumes directly: NetworkTaps.restAssured(service),
             which retires the StoryNetworkFilter every service had hand-copied, and the negative
             assertions (assertNoEdgesFrom / assertNoEdgesTo / assertOnlyEdgesFrom /
             assertEdgeCount) that let a story pin what did NOT happen. It also validates a
             declared edge's fields against Labels.scrub — nothing here declares one. See
             AGENTS.md, "The network diagram is observed, never narrated". -->
        <qits.userflows.version>2026.905.91808</qits.userflows.version>
        <!-- The recording service mocks the same IT boots against (the generic MockService plus
             idp.MockIdp), released out of libs/qits-integrations-quarkus like qits-db-core above
             (the same-string policy applies the day this repo consumes a newer reactor).
             2026.829.201505 is what makes a recorded request carry the STATUS the mock answered
             with, which is the half TokenValidationBootstrapIT's far-side edge label needs: a
             method and a path say the keys were asked for, the status says they were served. -->
        <qits.service-mock.version>2026.905.91442</qits.service-mock.version>
        <qits.maven.repository.url>http://registry.dev.localhost:8080/artifacts/maven/maven</qits.maven.repository.url>
        <maven.compiler.release>25</maven.compiler.release>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>

        <quarkus.platform.artifact-id>quarkus-bom</quarkus.platform.artifact-id>
        <quarkus.platform.group-id>io.quarkus.platform</quarkus.platform.group-id>
        <quarkus.platform.version>3.34.6</quarkus.platform.version>

        <compiler-plugin.version>3.15.0</compiler-plugin.version>
        <surefire-plugin.version>3.5.4</surefire-plugin.version>
        <jandex-plugin.version>3.4.0</jandex-plugin.version>
        <lombok.version>1.18.38</lombok.version>
        <lombok-mapstruct-binding.version>0.2.0</lombok-mapstruct-binding.version>
        <mapstruct.version>1.6.3</mapstruct.version>
        <!-- Quinoa is a Quarkiverse extension: not in quarkus-bom either, and its version does NOT
             track the platform's. 2.8.2 is built against Quarkus 3.27.3 LTS — older than the 3.34.6
             above, which is the direction that works, since a Quarkus extension compiled against an
             older core runs on a newer one. 2.8.3 is built against 3.36.2 and would be an extension
             asking this core for API it may not have. Bump it only past a platform bump. -->
        <quinoa.version>2.8.2</quinoa.version>
        <!-- Not in the platform BOM either. Reads the tar inside a docs bundle's .tar.gz; the gzip
             half is the JDK's. Pure stream parsing with no reflection, so it needs nothing
             registered for the native image — which `mvn verify -Dnative` is what proves. -->
        <commons-compress.version>1.28.0</commons-compress.version>
        <failsafe-plugin.version>${surefire-plugin.version}</failsafe-plugin.version>

        <!-- REAL postgres for the test suites: binaries resolved as ordinary Maven artifacts and
             run as a child process, so a clone still builds and tests green with no docker. The
             blob store's only backend is PostgreSQL now, and this service's schema is a PostgreSQL
             lineage, so H2 cannot stand in for either. 18.4.0 matches the platform's own
             qits-oci-postgresql image, and the same pair the qits-blobstore, qits-registries,
             qits-workspaces and qits-githost suites name. -->
        <zonky.embedded-postgres.version>2.2.2</zonky.embedded-postgres.version>
        <zonky.postgres-binaries.version>18.4.0</zonky.postgres-binaries.version>

        <!-- Integration tests run against a PACKAGED artifact. The library modules keep this
             default; the `service` module opts back IN (skipITs=false there), so a plain
             `mvn verify` boots the packaged fast-jar for its ITs — deliberately, because
             TokenValidationBootstrapIT is also the generator of the userstories documentation.
             The `native` profile keeps flipping it too, so `-Dnative` exercises the binary. -->
        <skipITs>true</skipITs>
    </properties>

    <dependencyManagement>
        <dependencies>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${quarkus.platform.group-id}</groupId>
                <artifactId>${quarkus.platform.artifact-id}</artifactId>
                <version>${quarkus.platform.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Which postgres the embedded binaries ARE. Imported as a BOM because the
                     per-arch artifacts are separate coordinates. -->
                <groupId>io.zonky.test.postgres</groupId>
                <artifactId>embedded-postgres-binaries-bom</artifactId>
                <version>${zonky.postgres-binaries.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.zonky.test</groupId>
                <artifactId>embedded-postgres</artifactId>
                <version>${zonky.embedded-postgres.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                <version>${lombok.version}</version>
                <scope>provided</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
                <artifactId>mapstruct</artifactId>
                <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.quarkiverse.quinoa</groupId>
                <artifactId>quarkus-quinoa</artifactId>
                <version>${quinoa.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.apache.commons</groupId>
                <artifactId>commons-compress</artifactId>
                <version>${commons-compress.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <!-- The shared byte-plane libraries. `qits-blobstore` is the content-addressed store
                 (repository/record entities, disk index, census inputs, and the OPEN repository-type
                 registration every profile bean plugs into); the three `qits-registries` modules
                 carry one package format each, both halves of it — hosted and pull-through cache —
                 because the two share a table and a set of routes. This service wires only the
                 hosted halves; the cache profiles are excluded from bean discovery in
                 service/src/main/resources/application.properties. -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-blobstore</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.blobstore.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-registries-common</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.registries.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-registries-npm</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.registries.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-registries-maven</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.registries.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-registries-oci</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.registries.version}</version>
            </dependency>

            <!-- The reactor's own modules, so `service` depends on them version-less. -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-artifacts-artifacts</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-artifacts-gc</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Published by qits-integrations-quarkus into the platform Maven repository. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-auth-core</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.auth-core.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- PatientPgDriver and DbRetry, from the same publisher. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-db-core</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.db-core.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Test scope at every declaration site: the story framework runs in the build
                     and ships in nothing. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-userflows</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.userflows.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Test scope at every declaration site, like qits-userflows. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-service-mock</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.service-mock.version}</version>
            </dependency>
        </dependencies>
    </dependencyManagement>

    <repositories>
        <repository>
            <id>qits-maven</id>
            <url>${qits.maven.repository.url}</url>
        </repository>
    </repositories>

    <build>
        <pluginManagement>
            <plugins>
                <plugin>
                    <groupId>${quarkus.platform.group-id}</groupId>
                    <artifactId>quarkus-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${quarkus.platform.version}</version>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${compiler-plugin.version}</version>
                    <configuration>
                        <parameters>true</parameters>
                        <!-- Incremental compilation leaves stale MapStruct *Impl classes behind
                             when a mapper's shape changes; the monorepo disables it for the same
                             reason. -->
                        <useIncrementalCompilation>false</useIncrementalCompilation>
                        <annotationProcessorPaths>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                                <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                                <version>${lombok.version}</version>
                            </path>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
                                <artifactId>mapstruct-processor</artifactId>
                                <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
                            </path>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                                <artifactId>lombok-mapstruct-binding</artifactId>
                                <version>${lombok-mapstruct-binding.version}</version>
                            </path>
                        </annotationProcessorPaths>
                    </configuration>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${surefire-plugin.version}</version>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <!-- `service` binds it; declared here so the version lives with surefire's. -->
                    <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${failsafe-plugin.version}</version>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <groupId>io.smallrye</groupId>
                    <artifactId>jandex-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${jandex-plugin.version}</version>
                    <executions>
                        <execution>
                            <id>make-index</id>
                            <goals>
                                <goal>jandex</goal>
                            </goals>
                        </execution>
                    </executions>
                </plugin>
            </plugins>
        </pluginManagement>
    </build>
</project>
